# Ship one change per commit

When the user says "ship", commit the work one change at a time. Do not put unrelated changes in one commit.

- One commit per change (a feature, a fix, or a schema change).
- Use a short `-m` message that says what changed.
- Then push those commits.

```text
Target Windows 10 for the chart libraries.
Remove product barcodes.
Save pickup or delivery with each sale.
```

Do not use one message that bundles several changes together.
